<title>ARGENTINA: Citibank Argentina buys remainder of pension group.</title>
<headline>Citibank Argentina buys remainder of pension group.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank's local unit announced Thursday it raised its stake in Argentine pension and insurance group Siembra to 100 percent after buying a remaining 51 percent stake for $230-$250 million.</p>
<p>Citibank Argentina President Carlos Fedrigotti told reporters the vendor was local Banco Rio. Last month, Spain's Banco Santander bought a controlling stake in Banco Rio.  </p>
<p>Siembra group comprises pension fund firm Siembra AFJP SA, insurer Sur Compania de Seguros de Vida SA and voluntary retirement savings company Siembra Compania de Seguros de Retiro SA.</p>
<p>((--Jorge Otaola, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0651))</p>
